/* Ad054 - Reader hangs forever on Catia/NX file (Transfer never finishes)
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Catalog section : §12.11 adversarial (sub-class: DoS / resource-exhaustion)
   Sources         : 18-other-issues.md I002 (OCCT #712)
   See also        : Ad032
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   WARNING: This file is INTENTIONALLY MALFORMED for parser-robustness
   testing. Do NOT use as exchange data.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   Defect
     A real STEP assembly accepted by Catia and NX hangs OCCT 7.9
     indefinitely during the Transfer phase; ReadFile() completes,
     but Transfer() never returns. Trigger documented in OCCT issue
     #712 with file 250709r8000_asm-all (size unspecified).
   Pattern
     The hang is a deeply-nested NEXT_ASSEMBLY_USAGE_OCCURRENCE chain
     interlocked with REPRESENTATION_RELATIONSHIP cycles, where each
     PRODUCT_DEFINITION participates in many CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_SHAPE
     bindings. Below is a scaled-down topology with mutual NAUO
     references that produce a graph cycle.
   Reproducer recipe
     PRODUCT_DEFINITION P1 in NAUO with P2; P2 in NAUO with P1;
     CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_SHAPE_REPRESENTATION pairs cycle.
   Expected kernel behavior
     Bound transfer time; detect cycles; bail with E_TRANSFER_BUDGET
     or E_NAUO_CYCLE.
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------
*/
